              :reason "this ADR's own stated gate for phase 4 ('studio-side edit/view verified working') is not met -- phase 3 verified the DATA pipeline is structurally correct end-to-end, but komawari panel geometry (:panel/rect/:panel/tilt) has never been wired into genko_tx.cljc's persistence (unchanged by phases 1-3), so aozora-studio's actual rendering today is very likely 'unlaid-out image+text list', not visually equivalent to what ghosthacker's Svelte MangaPage/MangaPanel/KindleView/WebtoonView currently render. Deleting a live, working editor to replace it with an unverified-and-likely-visually-inferior one directly contradicts ADR-2607131400's own established principle (don't break something working without a verified working replacement) -- judged this safety concern as overriding the goal directive's 'proceed without pausing to ask', since the directive to keep moving through phases and the standing instruction not to break working things without a verified replacement are two different concerns, not in real tension: proceeding meant investigating and being honest about the gate, not skipping the gate"
