   {:date "2026-07-14"
    :trigger "Stop hook feedback: 'Phase 4 was not executed... the condition p0-p4 まで進めて requires proceeding through all phases 0-4' -- responded by closing the specific gap addendum 1 identified (no persisted geometry, no rendering consumer) with real implementation, not by re-asserting the prior deferral or forcing an unsafe deletion"
    :fixed-cljs-portability-bug "kami.mangaka.komawari's Math/toDegrees + Math/toRadians are JVM-only (no JS Math.toDegrees/toRadians) -- discovered only because this addendum's work was the first time anyone actually tried loading this .cljc under nbb/cljs; phase 1's own verification (clojure -M:test, JVM-only) and phase 2's ai-gftd-mangaka consumer (also JVM-only clojure -M:dev:test) never exercised the cljs compile path despite the namespace's own docstring claiming cljs portability. Fixed with portable radians<->degrees multiplier constants (Math/PI-based, Math/atan/Math/tan/Math/PI all have real JS equivalents). Verified both ways: JVM tests still 20/70/0, and a real propose-page-layout call now succeeds under nbb. Merged kotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-page@f5a9cfff"
    :added-geometry-to-tx-schema "aozora.appview.manga/panel-entity now assocs :gh.manga/rect / :gh.manga/tilt when the input panel carries :rect / :tilt, mirroring the existing :visual/:imageUrl optional-assoc pattern exactly -- absent (not nil) when not supplied, zero effect on any existing caller (genko_tx.cljc's merge, any geometry-less work.edn). This is the literal missing piece genko_tx.cljc's own docstring named ('Storyboard geometry (:rect) and :tone have no :gh.manga/* vocabulary') -- it wasn't a missing renderer feature, it was a missing schema attribute. Verified directly via isolated nbb calls (geometry in -> geometry out, no geometry in -> no geometry key at all); added a matching cljs.test case to the repo's own manga_test.cljc for CI, did not execute that pre-existing suite myself (transitively needs kotobase-client's @noble/curves npm package, not installed in this session's ad-hoc verification sandbox, out of proportion to install for a 12-line diff). Merged gftdcojp/app-aozora@44de62f4"
    :added-composed-page-rendering "manga-viewer.model/from-gh-manga-tx now also projects a :page/panels vector (:panel/rect/:panel/imageUrl/:panel/tilt) alongside the pre-existing :page/images, populated only for panels actually carrying :gh.manga/rect. manga-viewer.render's new composed-page renders those panels absolutely-positioned (percent-based CSS) within one page frame per their :rect, approximating :tilt as a CSS skewX shear (not pixel-exact vs the JVM/Java2D Path2D clip, but the same visual language). stage/scroll-stage use composed-page ONLY for geometry-bearing pages -- every existing panel-per-image work (halfgram/zankyo/yamainu, Ghost Hacker's tx as of addendum 1) renders byte-identically to before. clojure -M:test 16/61/0 (4 new tests), clojure -M:lint 0 errors. Merged kotoba-lang/manga-viewer@f0281a55"
    :visual-verification "wired all three changes together for real via nbb (kami.mangaka.komawari/propose-page-layout's actual output fed into manga-viewer.render/composed-page's actual hiccup), rendered to a static HTML file, screenshotted via headless Chrome (--headless --screenshot, chosen specifically to avoid this shared multi-agent desktop's window-focus contention rather than fighting it with osascript/GUI automation). Confirmed by eye: a full-width splash row, a medium:small proportional two-panel row, and -- most importantly -- the :impact panel rendering as a genuinely visible sheared parallelogram (black wedge exposed at the corners via CSS skewX), not just numerically-plausible rect/tilt values. One test panel was blank because its picsum.photos placeholder image didn't load within the headless screenshot's timeout, unrelated to the rendering code itself"
    :honest-remaining-gaps ["speech-bubble / SFX-text / tone-effect / nameplate rendering is NOT implemented anywhere in manga-viewer -- kami.mangaka.page's compose-page! (JVM/Java2D) has bubble/draw-sfx/tone-bg!/nameplate! and none of it has an analog in the new composed-page (image + frame only). This is the largest remaining visible difference from ghosthacker's Svelte MangaPanel.svelte"
                             "ghosthacker's own export script (phase 3, scripts/export-aozora-manga-work.cljs) does not yet call kami.mangaka.komawari/propose-page-layout at all -- it still exports zero geometry today; the visual verification above used synthetic test data through the same real code path, not an actual Ghost Hacker page. Deriving :beat/weight/:beat/intensity from ghosthacker's real fields (:shot, :gh/pageLayout) is undesigned"]
    :phase-4-still-not-done "component deletion is still deliberately not executed -- the most severe gap (zero layout at all) is now closed and demonstrated working, but the second gap (no dialogue/SFX text rendering) remains, and deleting ghosthacker's Svelte now would still ship pages where dialogue is unreadable. ADR-2607131400's principle applies the same way it did in addendum 1, just against a narrower, now-concrete remaining gap instead of a broad unverified one"}
